  "sources": [
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "abilities",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "Passive",
          "name": "Holy Vanguard",
          "desc": "Invokes the protection of the divine light to recover Health continuously. If Movement Speed is impaired, the Health restored is doubled."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 1",
          "name": "Valiant Charge",
          "desc": "Enhances the next Basic Attack into a dash, dealing extra damage and silencing enemies."
        },
        {
          "type": "Skill 2",
          "name": "Whirling Strike",
          "desc": "Deals damage over time to nearby enemies."
        },
        {
          "type": "Ultimate",
          "name": "Might of Excalibur",
          "desc": "Jumps to the target enemy hero to deal damage. Launches all heroes within range."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "HOKFIRE",
      "url": "https://www.hokfire.com/",
      "field": "guide",
      "content": {
        "pros": [
          "Simple kit to learn",
          "In-built sustain",
          "Strong lane phase"
        ],
        "cons": [
          "Can be kited easily",
          "Struggles to reach the back line",
          "Limited damage"
        ],
        "gameplay_tips": "## Early Game\nSkill 2, Whirling Strike, can help you clear the first minion wave quickly to get level 2 before your opponent, giving you an advantage that you can use to win early trades. You want to take short trades so you can heal back up from your Passive every time. Each short chip of damage will help you win the Early Game. With this early advantage, you can look to secure Space Sprite and roam to help your team.\n\n## Teamfights\nTeamfights are a struggle for Arthur. You don't have a lot of mobility, so it's difficult for you to get onto the back line with your Ultimate and Skill 1. Try to stay in bushes to surprise the enemy carries and use your silence to stop high-impact skills on the enemy team. Always stay close enough to your team so they can back up your engage, and don't chase too far, as you can be kited very easily.\n\n## Tips & Tricks\nStart trades with Skill 1 for more damage on your auto attacks and other skills\nYou can auto attack after using Skill 1 to dash anywhere even over walls"
      }
    },
    {
      "source": "Kurohiko",
      "url": "https://hok.kurohiko.id/",
      "field": "tactical_tips",
      "content": "1) Melee di lane jangan adu poke sama Arthur, pasti kalah. 2) Hero ranged bisa poke dia. 3) Pas HP rendah jauhin Arthur, ult-nya sakit banget buat target sekarat."
    },
